From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:52:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_mpd: dump the WCSS region when the
 firmware crashes

The multi-PD WCSS driver registered no coredump segments and left
coredumps disabled, so a crash of the IPQ5018's WLAN firmware left no
dump at all, unlike the PCI radios'. Add the whole WCSS memory region as
a segment on each boot (it holds the firmware's memory and the M3 dump
area the WLAN firmware fills when it crashes), copied from the driver's
existing mapping by physical offset.

The dump is built in memory before the recovery goes on, not read
inline: an inline dump holds the recovery until userspace has read the
region, and ath11k gives up on the restarted firmware after waiting 10 s
for its memory request, which left the radio down.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
index 1e49a7da3..22e0886a9 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
@@ -529,10 +529,33 @@ static const struct rproc_ops wcss_ops = {
 	.get_boot_addr = rproc_elf_get_boot_addr,
 };
 
+static void q6_wcss_copy_segment(struct rproc *rproc,
+				 struct rproc_dump_segment *segment,
+				 void *dest, size_t offset, size_t size)
+{
+	struct q6_wcss *wcss = rproc->priv;
+
+	memcpy_fromio(dest, (void __iomem *)wcss->mem_region +
+		      (segment->da - wcss->mem_phys) + offset, size);
+}
+
+static int q6_wcss_parse_fw(struct rproc *rproc, const struct firmware *fw)
+{
+	struct q6_wcss *wcss = rproc->priv;
+
+	/* A crash dump holds the whole WCSS region: the firmware's memory
+	 * and the M3 dump area the WLAN firmware fills when it crashes.
+	 */
+	return rproc_coredump_add_custom_segment(rproc, wcss->mem_phys,
+						 wcss->mem_size,
+						 q6_wcss_copy_segment, NULL);
+}
+
 static const struct rproc_ops q6_wcss_ops = {
 	.start = q6_wcss_start,
 	.stop = q6_wcss_stop,
 	.da_to_va = q6_wcss_da_to_va,
+	.parse_fw = q6_wcss_parse_fw,
 	.load = q6_wcss_load,
 	.get_boot_addr = rproc_elf_get_boot_addr,
 	.panic = q6_wcss_panic,
@@ -806,6 +829,8 @@ static int q6_wcss_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	qcom_add_ssr_subdev(rproc, &wcss->ssr_subdev, "q6wcss");
 
 	rproc->auto_boot = false;
+	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_ENABLED;
+	rproc_coredump_set_elf_info(rproc, ELFCLASS32, EM_NONE);
 	ret = rproc_add(rproc);
 	if (ret)
 		goto free_rproc;
